### HVAC AI receptionist demo: the whole pipeline without a voice call.
#
# This is the fallback for demo day. If the audio fails, if the phone number
# will not connect, or if the Render instance is cold and the room is waiting,
# run these requests from top to bottom and every panel fills in exactly as it
# would during a real call: signature step, triage, service area check, customer
# match, arrival windows, the job on the dispatch board, the technician page,
# the caller confirmation, and the call outcome.
#
# Needs the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client). Click the
# "Send Request" link that appears above each ### block.
#
# BEFORE YOU START
#   1. Set ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS=true in .env.local, or in the Render
#      environment, and restart the app. Without it every request below comes
#      back 401, because none of them carry an x-retell-signature header.
#   2. Reset the demo so the seeded week is clean (request 1).
#   3. Switch @host below to whichever environment you are demonstrating.
#
# AFTERWARDS, set ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS back to false. It is a demo escape
# hatch and nothing else.

@host = http://localhost:3000
# @host = https://hvac-demo.onrender.com

# One call id ties every request below into a single call on the dashboard.
# Change it if you want a second, separate call on the timeline.
@callId = call_demo_fallback_001

# The caller for the main run. This number is NOT in the seeded customer book,
# so find_or_create_customer takes the create path, which is the more
# interesting one to show. Karen Dolan on +13125550188 is seeded, use that
# number instead if you want the "good to hear from you again" match path.
@caller = +13125550199
@line = +13125550137


### 1. Reset the demo to a fresh week
POST {{host}}/api/reset
Content-Type: application/json

###


### 2. Is the tool endpoint reachable, and is the signature check off?
# Expect: { "ok": true, "signature_required": false }
# If signature_required is true, ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS is not set and every
# request below will return 401.
GET {{host}}/api/retell/tool

###


### 3. Call starts. Opens the call row so the dashboard has something to draw.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_started",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "{{caller}}",
    "to_number": "{{line}}",
    "call_type": "phone_call"
  }
}

###


### 4. triage_problem, on the caller's own words.
# Expect urgency emergency, reason "no heat", job_type "no_heat",
# dispatch_tonight true, three qualifying questions, and a say line.
# The urgency badge should flip to EMERGENCY the moment this lands.
# @name triage
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "triage_problem",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "{{caller}}",
    "to_number": "{{line}}"
  },
  "args": {
    "description": "my furnace is dead and there's no heat"
  }
}

###


### 5. check_service_area, covered. Runs before anything is created.
# Expect: { "covered": true, "town": "Arlington Heights", "say": "Yes, we cover Arlington Heights." }
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "check_service_area",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "{{caller}}" },
  "args": { "postal_code": "60004" }
}

###


### 5b. check_service_area, not covered. Scene two, the out of area decline.
# Expect: { "covered": false, "say": "We do not cover Chicago, Lincoln Park, ..." }
# Nothing is written to dispatch on this path, which is the whole point.
# Send this one under its own call id if you want it as a separate call row.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "check_service_area",
  "call": { "call_id": "call_demo_fallback_002", "from_number": "+17735550144" },
  "args": { "postal_code": "60614" }
}

###


### 6. find_or_create_customer. No match on this number, so it creates one.
# Expect: { "status": "created", "client_id": "...", "property_id": "...", "first_name": "Dana" }
# The town is filled in from the postcode, so city can be left empty.
# @name customer
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "find_or_create_customer",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "{{caller}}" },
  "args": {
    "first_name": "Dana",
    "last_name": "Mercer",
    "street": "1402 South Highland Avenue",
    "city": "",
    "postal_code": "60004",
    "phone": ""
  }
}

###


### 7. get_arrival_windows. At most three, each with the exact words to speak.
# Expect: { "windows": [ { "id": "...", "say": "tonight between 8:00 PM and 10:00 PM with Dave" } ] }
# or { "status": "none_available" } if the seeded board happens to be full.
# @name windows
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "get_arrival_windows",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "{{caller}}" },
  "args": {
    "urgency": "emergency",
    "job_type": "no_heat"
  }
}

###


### 8. book_visit, using the first window get_arrival_windows just returned.
# The window id carries its own start time, technician and duration, so no
# server side state is needed between the two requests.
# Expect: { "status": "booked", "say": "...", "job_id": "..." }
# { "status": "queued" } means the write could not land, which is the failure
# path the agent turns into a callback rather than a dead end.
# @name booking
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "book_visit",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "{{caller}}" },
  "args": {
    "window_id": "{{windows.response.body.$.windows[0].id}}",
    "client_id": "{{customer.response.body.$.client_id}}",
    "property_id": "{{customer.response.body.$.property_id}}",
    "urgency": "emergency",
    "job_type": "no_heat",
    "symptom": "Furnace dead since this morning, thermostat calling for heat, unit about twelve years old"
  }
}

###


### 9. notify_on_call. Pages the technician and texts the caller.
# Expect: { "status": "notified", "technician": "..." }
# The technician is only paged for emergency work that is genuinely after
# hours, so during office hours this queues for the morning dispatch instead.
# Both texts appear on the phone mock up while Twilio is still in preview mode.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "notify_on_call",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "{{caller}}" },
  "args": {
    "urgency": "emergency",
    "summary": "No heat, furnace dead, 1402 South Highland Avenue, Arlington Heights",
    "window": "{{booking.response.body.$.say}}",
    "caller_phone": ""
  }
}

###


### 9b. Optional: log_estimate_request, scene four, the quote request.
# An estimate never books a technician. It creates a request for the team who
# sell replacements. Send it under its own call id to keep the timeline clean.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "log_estimate_request",
  "call": { "call_id": "call_demo_fallback_003", "from_number": "+13125550173" },
  "args": {
    "client_id": "cli_005",
    "property_id": "prop_005",
    "details": "Wants a price on a full system replacement. Current furnace about eighteen years old, single family home, roughly 2200 square feet."
  }
}

###


### 10. Call ends.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_ended",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "{{caller}}",
    "to_number": "{{line}}",
    "disconnection_reason": "user_hangup"
  }
}

###


### 11. Call analyzed. The outcome and the analysis fields land here.
# These four field names match post_call_analysis_data in retell/demo-agent.json.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_analyzed",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "{{caller}}",
    "to_number": "{{line}}",
    "call_analysis": {
      "call_summary": "Caller had no heat. Triaged as an emergency, postcode confirmed in the service area, new customer created, visit booked tonight and the on call technician paged.",
      "user_sentiment": "Positive",
      "call_successful": true,
      "custom_analysis_data": {
        "outcome": "booked",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "service_area_ok": true,
        "technician_paged": true
      }
    }
  }
}

###


### 11b. The out of area call, analyzed. Scene two on the outcome panel.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_analyzed",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "call_demo_fallback_002",
    "from_number": "+17735550144",
    "call_analysis": {
      "call_summary": "Caller in Lincoln Park. Postcode is outside the service area, so the assistant declined politely and offered to take a message. Nothing was sent to dispatch.",
      "user_sentiment": "Neutral",
      "call_successful": true,
      "custom_analysis_data": {
        "outcome": "out_of_area",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "service_area_ok": false,
        "technician_paged": false
      }
    }
  }
}

###


### 11c. The quote call, analyzed. Scene four on the outcome panel.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_analyzed",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "call_demo_fallback_003",
    "from_number": "+13125550173",
    "call_analysis": {
      "call_summary": "Caller wanted a price on a replacement system. Qualified on system age, property type and size, logged as an estimate request for the sales team. No technician booked and no price quoted.",
      "user_sentiment": "Positive",
      "call_successful": true,
      "custom_analysis_data": {
        "outcome": "estimate_request",
        "urgency": "quote",
        "service_area_ok": true,
        "technician_paged": false
      }
    }
  }
}

###


### 12. Read the state the panels draw from, to confirm it all landed.
GET {{host}}/api/state

###


### 13. Public config, to confirm which mode Jobber and SMS are in.
# integrations.jobber.mode is mock until the three JOBBER_ variables are set
# and JOBBER_MODE is not forced to mock. integrations.sms.mode is preview until
# the three TWILIO_ variables are set.
GET {{host}}/api/config

###
